window.AG_CHAPTERS["09"] = {"id":"09","title":"The Tea Stall Keeper","titleZh":"茶攤的杜大娘","patient":{"name":"Auntie Du 杜大娘","sprite":"girl"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-teahouse.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Heart and Spleen Both Deficient 心脾兩虛","principle":"strengthen the Spleen to make blood, and nourish the Heart to settle the spirit","tongue":"pale body, thin white coating, slightly swollen with tooth marks","pulseNote":{"en":"Narrow under the finger, and it gives way easily — thin, and without strength behind it.","zh":"脈道細小，按之無力，細而兼弱"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>T&#224;ib&#225;i SP3</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"SP3","zh":"太白","py":"T&#224;ib&#225;i","x":325,"y":966,"img":"art/body-leg-medial.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":0,"y":560,"w":434,"h":599},"decoys":[{"x":280,"y":964},{"x":196,"y":900},{"x":113,"y":868},{"x":178,"y":722},{"x":360,"y":948}],"note":"<b>太白 T&#224;ib&#225;i SP3</b> — on the medial border of the foot, in the depression proximal and inferior to the head of the first metatarsal bone, at the border between red and white flesh. Source point and Stream point of the Spleen.<br>足內側緣，第一蹠骨小頭後下方赤白肉際凹陷處。脾經原穴、輸穴。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Two households of symptoms live in this woman: one in the <b>chest and the sleep</b>, one in the <b>appetite and the stool</b>. Ask about both.","zh":"其症分居二處：一在胸中與睡眠，一在食慾與二便。二者俱當問。"},"look":{"en":"Look at the tongue <b>body</b> — its colour, and also its <b>shape</b>. A swollen edge that holds the print of the teeth says something the colour alone does not.","zh":"望舌質，觀其色，亦觀其形。舌胖有齒痕者，色所不能言也。"},"pulse":{"en":"Thin means the vessel is under-filled. Weak means there is no force pushing. She has both, and each points at a different lack.","zh":"細者脈道不充，弱者鼓動無力。二者並見，各指一虛。"},"dx":{"en":"Count the organs first, then find which one fell ill <b>first</b>, then say how this differs from the pattern you already know.","zh":"先數其臟，次尋其先病者，末辨其與已知之證何異。"},"rx":{"en":"You cannot fill the Heart directly. Fill the place where blood is <b>made</b>, and the Heart is fed by the same hand.","zh":"心不可徑補。補其生血之所，心自受其養。"},"tech":{"en":"Deficiency is reinforced. And ask yourself whether this patient — cold-handed, pale, loose in the bowel — could take a little warmth.","zh":"虛則補之。且自問：其人手冷面白便溏，可受溫否？"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen watches her count coins twice and get a different answer.","zh":"參師父看她數了兩遍錢，數出兩個數目。"},{"who":"patient","en":"Auntie Du presses the heel of her hand against her chest without noticing she is doing it.","zh":"杜大娘用掌根按著胸口，自己沒察覺。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy brings her a stool. She sits down more heavily than she meant to.","zh":"藥童搬了張凳子給她。她坐下時，比自己想的還沉。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"She has run that tea stall alone for eleven years,\" he says. \"Ask what she has been carrying.\"","zh":"「那茶攤她一個人撐了十一年，」他說，「問問她心裡擱著什麼。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"I lie down and my mind starts walking,\" she says. \"By the time it stops, the birds are up.\"","zh":"「一躺下，腦子就開始走路，」她說，「等它停下來，鳥都叫了。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Thought is the movement of the Spleen. Too much of it, and the Spleen does not eat, and then the blood does not come.\"","zh":"「思為脾之動。思之過度，脾不受納，血則無以生。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"excess_def","look":"excess_def","pulse":"excess_def","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"excess_def"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Feed the Source","cardZh":"補土生血，養心安神","cardTxt":"When the Heart is empty of blood and the Spleen is too weak to make more, treating the Heart alone empties it again by the next moon. Strengthen the earth that makes the blood, and the Heart is nourished from upstream.","herbId":"lianzi","herbEn":"Lotus Seed","herbZh":"蓮子","herbImg":"art/card-lianzi.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sweet, astringent and neutral. In TCM it both strengthens the Spleen and calms the spirit — one of the few foods traditionally said to speak to the Heart and the Spleen at the same time. It is eaten in congee and in sweet soups."},"endings":{"three":["A month later the tea stall opens on time again. \"I fall asleep before the lamp goes out now,\" Auntie Du says, and counts your change correctly on the first try.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You did not chase the sleeplessness. You went upstream and fed the thing that had stopped making blood. That is the difference between quieting a symptom and treating a person.\"","一個月後，茶攤又準時開了。「現在燈還沒滅我就睡著了，」杜大娘說，找錢一次就找對。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你沒有去追那個失眠。你往上游走，去補那個已經不生血的地方。安症與治人之別，正在於此。」"],"two":["She sleeps better, but her appetite is still small and the stool still loose.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You settled the spirit. You did not finish repairing the place the spirit is fed from.\"","她睡得好些了，胃口仍小，大便仍溏。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你安了神。生神之處，你還沒有修完。」"],"one":["No change. She is back at the stall before dawn, pale as before.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Two organs. You named one. Go back and count again.\"","沒有變化。她天沒亮又回到攤子上，面色依舊。<br><b>參師父：</b>「病涉二臟，你只舉了一臟。回去再數一次。」"],"titles":["Auntie Du Sleeps Through","Auntie Du Rests a Little","Auntie Du Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"You have treated blood deficiency once already. This patient will look very like that one. She is not.","cn":"你已治過一次血虛。這位病人看起來很像，其實不是。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. Du. I keep the tea stall by the north gate. I don't know what's wrong with me exactly — I'm just used up.","cn":"大夫。姓杜，北門口擺茶攤的。也說不上哪裡壞了，就是整個人被用完了。"},{"w":"patient","en":"My heart flutters when I stand up. I can't sleep, and when I do I dream all night. And I forget things I only just said.","cn":"一站起來心就跳得慌。睡不著，睡著了整夜作夢。剛說過的話轉頭就忘。"},{"w":"master","en":"Palpitations, insomnia, poor memory — those are the Heart's complaints. Note them, then do not stop there.","cn":"心悸、失眠、健忘，此心之所苦。記下，但不要就此打住。"},{"w":"master","en":"Ask her about her food and her stool. If a second organ is involved, that is where it will answer you.","cn":"問其飲食與二便。若病涉二臟，答案在此。"}],"qa":[{"q":"How is your appetite, and how do you feel after eating?","cq":"胃口如何？飯後覺得怎樣？","good":1,"a":"I eat very little, and afterwards I feel bloated and want to lie down.","ca":"吃得很少，飯後脹，就想躺下。","clue":{"en":"Poor appetite, bloating and fatigue after meals","zh":"納少、食後腹脹倦怠"},"note":"This is the Spleen, plainly. A pure blood deficiency does not fail at the table. Poor intake, fullness after food and sleepiness after meals are the classic reading of a Spleen that can no longer transform. 此明是脾。單純血虛者不礙於食。納少、食後脹滿、飯後思睡，正脾失健運之常象。"},{"q":"What are your stools like?","cq":"大便怎麼樣？","good":1,"a":"Loose, most days. Sometimes I can see the food in them.","ca":"多半是溏的，有時還見得到沒消化的東西。","clue":{"en":"Loose stool with undigested food","zh":"便溏、完穀不化"},"note":"Loose stool with undigested food is the Spleen failing to transform, not the Heart. Two organs are now on the table, and this is the second one. 便溏、完穀不化，脾失運化，非心之事。至此二臟俱見。"},{"q":"Has something been weighing on your mind?","cq":"心裡是不是有事一直擱著？","good":1,"a":"My son went to the capital three years ago. I think about it every night.","ca":"兒子三年前去了京裡。我每晚都在想這件事。","clue":{"en":"Prolonged overthinking and worry","zh":"思慮過度"},"note":"<b>This is the cause, and it decides the order of the pattern.</b> In TCM the Spleen governs thought; sustained worry knots the Spleen qi, the Spleen stops making blood, and the Heart — which stores the spirit in blood — is left unfed. Spleen first, Heart second. 此為病因，且定其先後。脾主思，思慮不解則脾氣結，脾不生血，心血失養而神不藏。脾先而心後。"},{"q":"Do you bruise easily, or bleed for a long time from a small cut?","cq":"容易瘀青嗎？小傷口血止得慢嗎？","good":1,"a":"I bruise on the arms without knowing how. And my monthly flow drags on, pale and thin.","ca":"手臂常莫名其妙瘀青。月經拖得長，色淡而稀。","clue":{"en":"Easy bruising, prolonged pale menses","zh":"易瘀斑、經期延長色淡"},"note":"An excellent question. The Spleen governs the blood and holds it in the vessels; when it is too weak to hold, blood seeps out where it should not. This finding belongs to the Spleen, not the Heart, and it strengthens the case for two organs. 問得極好。脾統血，虛則不能攝血，血溢脈外。此症屬脾不屬心，益證二臟同病。"},{"q":"Do you have night sweats and a warm flush in the afternoons?","cq":"有盜汗嗎？午後潮熱嗎？","good":0,"a":"No. If anything I'm cold — my hands are cold even in the shop.","ca":"沒有。反倒是怕冷，在店裡手都是涼的。","clue":"","note":"A clean exclusion, and worth making. Those two findings would mean yin deficiency with empty heat. There is no heat anywhere in this case — which is why moxa will be permitted here and was forbidden two patients ago. 排除得當，且有其必要。此二症屬陰虛內熱。本案通身無熱，故此處可灸，而前二案不可。"}],"look":[{"t":"Pale body, slightly swollen, with tooth marks along the edge","c":"舌淡胖、邊有齒痕","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Pale swollen tongue with tooth marks","zh":"舌淡胖有齒痕"},"note":"Correct, and it is two findings again. Pale = blood does not fill the tongue. Swollen with tooth marks = Spleen qi too weak to move fluids, so the tongue presses against the teeth. Colour gives you the Heart's problem; shape gives you the Spleen's. 是，此亦二象。淡者血不榮舌；胖而有齒痕者，脾氣虛不運水濕，舌體壓於齒。色見心之病，形見脾之病。"},{"t":"Pale body with a thin white coat, normal shape","c":"舌淡苔薄白，形正","ok":0,"note":"That is the simple blood deficiency you saw in A-Xiu. It is close — but it misses the swelling and the tooth marks, which are exactly what tells you a second organ is involved. 此即阿秀之單純血虛。相去甚近，然漏卻胖與齒痕，而此二者正是二臟同病之憑。"},{"t":"Red body with little coating","c":"舌紅少苔","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat. Her tongue has no red in it and she is cold to the touch. 陰虛內熱之象。本案舌無紅色，其人肌膚亦涼。"},{"t":"Pale purple body with a white coat","c":"舌淡紫、苔白","ok":0,"note":"That would suggest cold with blood stasis. There is no fixed stabbing pain and no dark clotting — she seeps rather than stagnates. 此主寒凝血瘀。本案無定處刺痛、無紫黑血塊。其血溢而非瘀。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Thready and weak 細弱","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Thready weak pulse","zh":"脈細弱"},"note":"Correct, and once more it reads as two things at once. <b>Thready</b>: the vessel is not filled — blood is short. <b>Weak</b>: there is no force behind the beat — qi is short. Blood shortage and qi shortage in one pulse is the signature of this pattern. 是，一脈而見二事。細者脈道不充，血少也；弱者鼓動無力，氣虛也。氣血兩虛，見於一脈。"},{"t":"Thready and rapid 細數","ok":0,"note":"Thready is right, rapid is not. Rapid would add heat, and heat with deficiency means yin deficiency — the previous patient, not this one. 細是，數非。數則有熱，虛而有熱者屬陰虛，乃前案，非本案。"},{"t":"Deep and slow 沉遲","ok":0,"note":"That is interior cold — a yang deficiency or cold congealing. She is cold-handed, but there is no deep cold pain, no clear watery urine, no dawn diarrhoea. Not yet. 此屬裡寒，陽虛或寒凝。其手雖冷，然無冷痛、無小便清長、無五更瀉。尚未至此。"},{"t":"Slippery 滑","ok":0,"note":"Slippery means something substantial rolls in the vessel — phlegm, food, or pregnancy. This vessel is under-filled, which is the opposite. 滑者脈中有形之物往來，痰、食、或孕。本案脈道不充，適與之反。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — how many organs are involved?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：病涉幾臟？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Two — the Heart and the Spleen","c":"二臟 — 心與脾","ok":1,"note":"Correct. Sort her findings into two piles and neither pile is empty. <b>Heart:</b> palpitations, insomnia, dream-disturbed sleep, poor memory. <b>Spleen:</b> poor appetite, bloating after food, loose stool with undigested food, easy bruising, a swollen tongue with tooth marks. Two piles, two organs. 是。分其症為二，二者皆不空。心：心悸、失眠、多夢、健忘。脾：納少、食脹、便溏完穀不化、易瘀斑、舌胖齒痕。二堆，二臟。"},{"t":"One — the Heart alone","c":"一臟 — 獨在心","ok":0,"note":"Then what accounts for the appetite, the stool and the tooth marks? The Heart does not govern digestion. Half her findings would have nowhere to live. 若獨在心，則納呆、便溏、齒痕何屬？心不主運化。其症半數無處安放。"},{"t":"One — the Spleen alone","c":"一臟 — 獨在脾","ok":0,"note":"Then what accounts for the palpitations, the dreaming and the forgetting? The Spleen does not store the spirit. 若獨在脾，則心悸、多夢、健忘何屬？脾不藏神。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — of the two, which fell ill first?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：二臟之中，何者先病？</small>","opts":[{"t":"The Spleen — and the Heart followed","c":"脾先病，心從之","ok":1,"note":"<b>This is the step that decides the treatment.</b> Three years of unrelieved worry; in TCM the Spleen governs thought, so sustained worry knots Spleen qi first. A Spleen that cannot transform cannot make blood. The Heart stores the spirit in blood — with no blood arriving, the spirit has nowhere to rest, and you get palpitations, dreaming and forgetfulness. The chain runs <b>worry → Spleen → blood → Heart</b>. Treat the far end and the near end refills itself. 此步定治法。憂思三年不解；脾主思，思鬱則脾氣先結。脾不運化則血無以生。心藏神於血，血不至則神無所依，故心悸、多夢、健忘。其鏈為：思 → 脾 → 血 → 心。治其源，其末自復。"},{"t":"The Heart — and the Spleen followed","c":"心先病，脾從之","ok":0,"note":"Possible in principle, but not here. The history begins with worry, not with palpitations — and worry enters through the Spleen. If you reverse the chain you will treat the Heart, she will sleep for a fortnight, and the emptiness will return, because the source is still not making blood. 理雖可有，本案則非。其病始於憂思而非始於心悸，而思由脾入。若倒其序，但治其心，可安眠旬日，其虛必返，蓋生血之源未復。"},{"t":"They fell ill together, from the same cause","c":"二臟同時受病","ok":0,"note":"Tempting, and it is not far wrong — but it gives you no order of treatment, and order is what this case is teaching. A cause that enters through thought enters through the Spleen. 說法近似，然無先後則無次第，而次第正本案所教。從思而入者，必先入脾。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — how does this differ from the blood deficiency you already treated?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：此與前案之血虛何異？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Qi is short as well as blood — and the spirit is unsettled","c":"氣血兩虛，兼神不安","ok":1,"note":"Correct. A-Xiu was short of <b>blood</b>: pale face, pale lips, dizziness, thin pulse, a tongue pale but normal in shape. Auntie Du has all of that <b>plus</b> the qi signs — no appetite, loose stool, fullness after food, a swollen tongue with tooth marks, a pulse weak as well as thin — <b>plus</b> the spirit signs: palpitations, dreaming, forgetting. Same colour, more layers. 是。阿秀所虧者血：面唇淡白、頭暈、脈細、舌淡而形正。杜大娘兼見氣虛之象：納呆、便溏、食脹、舌胖齒痕、脈細而弱；又兼神不安：心悸、多夢、健忘。色同而層次多。"},{"t":"There is no real difference — it is blood deficiency in an older woman","c":"實無異，不過年長者之血虛","ok":0,"note":"Then you would nourish blood and stop. She would improve for a fortnight and slide back, because the organ that makes blood was never repaired. Age is not a diagnosis. 若然，則但養血而止。旬日稍安，其後必復，蓋生血之臟未修。年歲非證。"},{"t":"This one has heat and the earlier one did not","c":"此案有熱，前案無熱","ok":0,"note":"There is no heat here at all: no thirst, no night sweat, no red tongue, no rapid pulse, and her hands are cold. Read the case again before reaching for a difference that is not there. 本案全無熱象：不渴、不盜汗、舌不紅、脈不數，手且冷。求異當先讀案。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"SP3","t":"T&#224;ib&#225;i SP3 太白","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Spleen, and its Stream point. When the organ itself is depleted rather than obstructed, the Source point is where you go. This is the point that repairs the far end of the chain — the earth that makes the blood. 脾之原穴，亦其輸穴。臟自虧而非邪阻者，取原穴。此穴修其鏈之遠端，即生血之土。"},{"id":"ST36","t":"Z&#250;s&#257;nl&#464; ST36 足三里","ok":1,"note":"Sea point of the Stomach and the great tonifying point of the middle burner. Spleen and Stomach are the source of acquired qi and blood; strengthen them and you are filling the jar rather than pouring from it. It is also the classic point to moxa in a cold, empty patient. 胃之合穴，補中焦之要穴。脾胃為後天氣血生化之源，補之如注水入罐，非取水於罐。虛寒者，此穴尤宜灸。"},{"id":"PC6","t":"N&#232;igu&#257;n PC6 內關","ok":1,"note":"Connecting point of the Pericardium and confluent point of the Yin Wei mai. It is the point for palpitations and an unsettled spirit — the near end of the chain. Using it with SP3 and ST36 treats the symptom and the source in one prescription. 心包絡穴，八脈交會通陰維。主心悸、安神，治其鏈之近端。與太白、足三里同用，標本兼顧。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Y&#299;nl&#237;ngqu&#225;n SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Drains damp from the lower burner, and it drains. There is no damp here — no heavy limbs, no greasy coat, no swelling — and draining an already empty patient takes what little she has. 利下焦之濕，其法主瀉。本案無濕：不身重、苔不膩、無浮腫。虛者瀉之，是奪其僅存。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"T&#224;ich&#333;ng LR3 太衝","ok":0,"note":"Soothes the Liver and moves qi. She is worried, so the reach for the Liver is understandable — but worry that enters through thought is the Spleen's burden, not the Liver's, and strong qi-moving disperses qi she cannot spare. 疏肝行氣。其人有憂，故取肝可解；然思傷脾而非傷肝，且強行氣則耗其所不足之氣。"},{"id":"ST40","t":"F&#275;ngl&#243;ng ST40 豐隆","ok":0,"note":"Transforms phlegm. There is no phlegm in this case, and the point is draining and drying by nature — the wrong direction for someone this empty. 化痰之穴。本案無痰，且其性瀉而燥，於虛者為逆。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method, with moxa","c":"補法，可施灸","ok":1,"note":"Correct on both counts, and the moxa is the point of contrast. Deficiency is reinforced. And <b>moxa is warming</b> — which was wrong for the dry yin-deficient patient and wrong for the hot phlegm patient, but is right here: she is pale, cold-handed and loose in the bowel, with no heat anywhere in the case. The question is never \"is she deficient?\" but \"deficient <b>and</b> cold, or deficient <b>and</b> hot?\" 二者皆是，而要義在灸。虛則補之。灸性溫：於陰虛之燥者不宜，於痰熱之實者不宜，於本案則宜——面白、手冷、便溏，通案無熱。所問者非「虛否」，而是「虛而寒」抑或「虛而熱」。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, but no moxa","c":"補法，不施灸","ok":0,"note":"Half right, and cautious — but it withholds the one thing that would help her most. Moxa is withheld when there is heat or dryness. She has neither. 半是，其慎可取，然所withheld者正其最需。有熱有燥則忌灸，本案二者皆無。"},{"t":"Reducing method to settle the palpitations","c":"瀉法以定其悸","ok":0,"note":"The palpitations come from emptiness, not from something pressing on the Heart. Draining an empty Heart makes the fluttering worse, not better. 其悸由虛而生，非有物迫心。心虛而瀉之，悸必更甚。"},{"t":"Even method, since two organs are involved","c":"平補平瀉，因病涉二臟","ok":0,"note":"Two organs does not mean a compromise technique. Both organs are <b>empty</b>. When everything in the case is deficient, reinforce. 病涉二臟，非謂手法當折中。二臟俱虛，通案皆虛者，補之而已。"}]};
